description:
FOUND (s526w1, URI t/escape.t row 19 "invalid range with max less than min throws exception": got undef).

Pl/ExprToCL.pm gen_funcall_form: the call HEAD is lowered by cl_name, which since #2100 sends a DECLARED (or imported, prototype-recorded) sub whose name is also in %RUNTIME_NAMES to `pl-NAME`; the call TAIL -- the #2636 copy-back test and the *wantarray* bind -- asked `$force_user || !exists $RUNTIME_NAMES{$func_name}` instead, so for such a sub it took the BUILT-IN branch: no bind, no copy-back.  As an argument of another call inside a void statement the sub saw *wantarray* = :void.  Test::Fatal::exception is `return try {...} catch {...}`, and Try::Tiny returns NOTHING in void context, so `show(exception { die "boom\n" })` passed undef.  Every `like exception { ... }, qr/.../` / `is exception {...}, undef` row in a CPAN test is behind it.

Probe (scratch p-guard3825.pl):
  sub exception (&) { my $c = shift; $c->(); wantarray ? "list" : defined(wantarray) ? "scalar" : "void" }
  sub hash { wantarray ? "L" : defined(wantarray) ? "S" : "V" }
  sub show { print join(",", @_), "\n" }
  show(exception { 1 }); show(exception { 1 }, "x"); show(hash(1), hash());
  my $s = hash(); my @l = (hash()); print "$s @l\n";
perl 5.40.3: list / list,x / L,L / S L.   base (main 706cfde8): void / void,x / V,V / S L.

FIX (s526w1 filler, one mechanism): one predicate `$user_call` computed right after `$cl_func` -- true when force_user, when the name is not a runtime name, or when cl_name lowered the head to `pl-NAME` -- and both tail sites ask it.  Guard Pl/t/runtime-name-hygiene-01.t row 5 (perl oracle).  Generation v2-8585.

DONE (s526w1): fixed as described above; bars in the s526w1 commit / report.
